<section class="hero" id="home"><div class="wrap hero-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow">A space for you. A step towards yourself.</div><h1>Be heard.<br>Be understood.<br><em>Be yourself.</em></h1><p class="lead">You don’t have to have it all figured out. Find a supportive space to explore what’s on your mind, at your own pace.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="#contact">Let’s take the first step <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="btn light" href="#services">Explore our services</a></div><div class="hero-note"><span>Established in 2011</span><span>Online & in-person sessions</span></div></div><div class="art"><img src="@endverbatim{{ asset('images/vidya-logo.png') }}@verbatim" alt="Vidya: a space for understanding and growth" width="310" height="310"><div class="since">SINCE<strong>2011</strong></div><div class="art-note">A little space. A new perspective.</div></div></div></section>
<div class="ribbon"><div class="wrap"><span>Career & education</span><b aria-hidden="true">✧</b><span>Mental wellbeing</span><b aria-hidden="true">✧</b><span>Marriage & family</span><b aria-hidden="true">✧</b><span>Support through life’s transitions</span></div></div>
<section id="services"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">How we can support you</div><h2>Different journeys.<br>Thoughtful support.</h2></div><p>Whether you’re facing a decision, a difficult season or a relationship challenge, there is room to talk.</p></div><div class="cards"><article class="card"><span class="num">01 / FINDING DIRECTION</span><h3>Career & Education<br>Counselling</h3><p>Make space to understand your interests, explore your choices and think about what comes next.</p><ul><li>Academic pressure and student concerns</li><li>Stream, course and career choices</li><li>Career exploration and transitions</li></ul><a class="textlink service-link" data-service="Career & Education Counselling" href="#contact">Explore your next step ↗</a></article><article class="card"><span class="num">02 / MAKING SPACE</span><h3>Mental Health<br>Counselling</h3><p>A supportive conversation about the feelings and experiences that may be difficult to carry alone.</p><ul><li>Stress and emotional concerns</li><li>Self-esteem and life transitions</li><li>Grief, loneliness and feeling overwhelmed</li></ul><a class="textlink service-link" data-service="Mental Health Counselling" href="#contact">Make space for yourself ↗</a></article><article class="card"><span class="num">03 / BUILDING CONNECTION</span><h3>Marriage & Family<br>Counselling</h3><p>Explore patterns, communication and the challenges that affect relationships and family life.</p><ul><li>Relationship and communication concerns</li><li>Parenting challenges</li><li>Family dynamics and understanding</li></ul><a class="textlink service-link" data-service="Marriage & Family Counselling" href="#contact">Start a conversation ↗</a></article></div></div></section>
<section class="about" id="about"><div class="wrap split"><div class="quote-panel"><div class="flower" aria-hidden="true">✳</div><blockquote>“A space where people feel heard, understood and accepted.”</blockquote><small>The purpose behind Vidya</small></div><div><div class="eyebrow">Meet the person behind the purpose</div><h2>A journey of listening.<br>A purpose of care.</h2><p class="role">TRUPTI KULSHRESHTHA · FOUNDER</p><p>Through her work with NGOs and vulnerable communities, Trupti saw how being heard and supported could make a difference. She also recognised the quieter emotional struggles in everyday life—in homes, schools, workplaces and relationships.</p><p>In 2011, she established Vidya Counselling Centre: a space where you don’t need to prove your concern is “serious enough” to ask for support.</p><p>Named in gratitude to her mother, Vidya carries a deeply personal meaning and a simple purpose: understanding people.</p><button class="btn light" data-dialog="story" style="margin-top:25px">Read Trupti’s story ↗</button></div></div></section>
<section class="audience"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">You are welcome here</div><h2>Support through different stages of life.</h2><div class="tags"><span>Students</span><span>Adolescents</span><span>Parents</span><span>Adults</span><span>Couples</span><span>Families</span><span>Working professionals</span></div></div></section>
<section id="approach"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">One step at a time</div><h2>A gentle beginning.</h2></div><p>You can begin with a simple enquiry. We’ll discuss your needs and the next steps together.</p></div><div class="steps"><article class="step"><b>01</b><h3>Reach out</h3><p>Let us know you’re interested and whether you prefer an online or in-person session.</p></article><article class="step"><b>02</b><h3>Find a time</h3><p>Discuss availability, session details and fees before confirming your appointment.</p></article><article class="step"><b>03</b><h3>Start talking</h3><p>Share what feels comfortable. Your first conversation is a chance to understand your concerns.</p></article><article class="step"><b>04</b><h3>Move forward</h3><p>Discuss your goals and appropriate next steps at a pace that works for you.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="modes" id="sessions"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Choose your space</div><h2>Here in Dombivli.<br>Or wherever you feel at ease.</h2></div></div><div class="modegrid"><article class="mode"><div class="eyebrow">01 / IN-PERSON</div><h3>A space away from the everyday.</h3><p>Visit Vidya Counselling Centre in Dombivli East for an in-person conversation. Sessions are arranged by appointment.</p><a href="#contact" class="textlink mode-link" data-mode="In-person">Request an in-person session ↗</a></article><article class="mode"><div class="eyebrow">02 / ONLINE</div><h3>Support, with a little more flexibility.</h3><p>Connect from a quiet, private space. Ask about online availability and suitability when you enquire.</p><a href="#contact" class="textlink mode-link" data-mode="Online">Request an online session ↗</a></article></div></div></section>
<section id="faq"><div class="wrap faq-layout"><div class="faq-intro"><div class="eyebrow">A little clarity</div><h2>It’s okay to<br>have questions.</h2><p>Starting something new can feel unfamiliar. Here are a few things you may want to know.</p><a class="textlink" href="#contact">Ask us a question ↗</a></div><div class="faqs"><details><summary>Do I need a serious problem to seek counselling?</summary><p>You can reach out when you want space to reflect, understand a concern or navigate a decision. You don’t need to wait until things feel overwhelming.</p></details><details><summary>What happens in the first session?</summary><p>The first conversation is an opportunity to discuss what brings you here, ask questions and explore what support may be appropriate. You can share at your own pace.</p></details><details><summary>Are online sessions available?</summary><p>Yes, both online and in-person consultations are offered. Availability, the platform and suitability for your circumstances can be discussed before confirmation.</p></details><details><summary>What are the fees and session timings?</summary><p>Please contact the centre for current fees, session duration and available appointment times. Sending an enquiry does not confirm a booking.</p></details><details><summary>Can I ask about privacy before a session?</summary><p>Yes. Ask about confidentiality, its limits and how your information is handled before starting. Please avoid sharing sensitive personal or medical details in an initial enquiry.</p></details><details><summary>Where is the centre located?</summary><p>Ground floor, Glory Apartment, Rajaji Path, opposite Abhinav Bank, Dombivli East, Kalyan, Maharashtra 421201. <a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/n5az4nX9wgc9NYG2A" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open Google Maps ↗</a></p></details></div></div></section>
<section class="contact" id="contact"><div class="wrap contactgrid"><div><div class="eyebrow">Let’s begin with a conversation</div><h2>Your first step<br>can be a small one.</h2><p class="intro">Reach out to ask a question or request a consultation. We’ll take it from there, together.</p><address>Vidya Counselling Centre<br>Ground floor, Glory Apartment, Rajaji Path,<br>opposite Abhinav Bank, Dombivli East,<br>Kalyan, Maharashtra 421201</address><a class="textlink" href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/n5az4nX9wgc9NYG2A" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Get directions ↗</a><div class="contact-links"><a href="tel:+919920392160">+91 99203 92160</a><a href="mailto:vidyacounsellingcenter@gmail.com">vidyacounsellingcenter@gmail.com</a></div><p style="font-size:12px;margin-top:25px">Online & in-person · By appointment</p></div><form class="contactform" id="enquiry"><h3>Request a consultation</h3><p class="hint">This form prepares a WhatsApp message. You review and send it yourself; it does not confirm an appointment. Please don’t include sensitive health information.</p><label>Your name<input name="name" autocomplete="name" maxlength="80" required placeholder="How should we address you?"></label><div class="fieldrow"><label>I’m interested in<select name="service" id="service"><option>Not sure yet</option>Career & Education Counselling</option><option>Mental Health Counselling</option><option>Marriage & Family Counselling</option></select></label><label>Session preference<select name="mode" id="mode"><option>No preference</option><option>In-person</option><option>Online</option></select></label></div><label class="consent"><input type="checkbox" required><span>I agree to share these details with the centre through WhatsApp. <a href="#" data-dialog="privacy">Privacy information</a></span></label><button type="submit" class="btn">Continue to WhatsApp <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button><p id="status" role="status"></p><noscript><p>JavaScript is disabled. Please use the phone or email links to contact the centre.</p></noscript></form></div></section>
</main>
<footer><div class="wrap"><div class="footrow"><div><strong>Vidya Counselling Centre</strong><p>A space to be heard, understood and supported.</p></div><div class="footlinks"><a href="https://www.instagram.com/vidya_counseling_center/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Instagram ↗</a><a href="https://www.facebook.com/vidyacounselingcentre" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Facebook ↗</a><button data-dialog="privacy">Privacy</button><button data-dialog="terms">Website information</button></div></div><div class="disclaimer"><p>© <span id="year">2026</span> Vidya Counselling Centre. All rights reserved. Counselling enquiries are not an emergency service. If you are in immediate danger, contact local emergency services or go to the nearest emergency department.</p></div></div></footer>
<a class="btn floating" href="#contact">Let’s talk ↗</a>
<dialog id="story"><button class="close" aria-label="Close story">Close ×</button><div class="eyebrow">Our story</div><h2>Trupti’s Story</h2><p><em>The journey behind Vidya Counselling Centre</em></p><div id="story-content"><p>For Trupti Kulshreshtha, psychology has never been just a profession. It has been a journey of understanding people, their struggles, their strengths, and the many different ways in which people experience life.</p><p>Over the course of her career, Trupti has had the opportunity to work with several NGOs and organisations, closely supporting people from vulnerable and challenging backgrounds. Her work brought her in contact with children and adolescents in crisis, children in conflict with the law, girls facing difficult circumstances, survivors of trauma and trafficking, and individuals dealing with complex emotional and social challenges.</p><p>These experiences gave Trupti a deep and meaningful understanding of human behaviour and resilience. Working closely with people who were going through some of the most difficult phases of their lives gave her immense professional satisfaction. She experienced firsthand how being heard, understood and supported could make a difference in someone&#x27;s life.</p><p>But while working with vulnerable communities, Trupti began noticing another reality around her.</p><p>She could see that mental health concerns were not limited to the people she was professionally working with. They were present all around her—in families, schools, workplaces and relationships.</p><p>Students were struggling with academic pressure and anxiety. Parents were overwhelmed by responsibilities. Couples were facing relationship difficulties. Working professionals were experiencing stress and emotional exhaustion. Many people were dealing with loneliness, grief, confusion and a loss of direction.</p><p>Yet, unlike many visible physical or social problems, these struggles were often difficult to notice.</p><p>People could appear completely fine on the outside while experiencing significant emotional difficulties within. Their problems were not always recognised by society, and sometimes they were not even recognised by the individuals themselves.</p><p>This created a growing restlessness within Trupti.</p><p>On one side, she was experiencing immense satisfaction through her NGO work and the opportunity to support vulnerable communities. On the other, she found herself deeply concerned about the psychological struggles she was witnessing among the general public.</p><p>She began to feel that there was a need for a space where people could seek psychological support before their difficulties became overwhelming—a space where a person did not need to prove that their problem was “serious enough” to ask for help.</p><p>This restlessness eventually became the inspiration for Vidya Counselling Centre, which Trupti established in 2011.</p><p>Vidya Counselling Centre became an extension of everything she had learned through her years of work. It gave her the opportunity to bring her experience of working with vulnerable populations into a space that was open to people from all walks of life.</p><p>The story behind “Vidya”</p><p>The name Vidya has a deeply personal meaning for Trupti.</p><p>Vidya was her mother&#x27;s name.</p><p>Although her mother is no longer with her, Trupti continues to carry a deep sense of gratitude towards her. Her mother&#x27;s presence, values and influence remain an important part of Trupti&#x27;s personal journey.</p><p>Choosing the name Vidya Counselling Centre was therefore not simply a professional decision. It was Trupti&#x27;s way of expressing her gratitude and keeping her mother&#x27;s name connected to something that is deeply meaningful to her.</p><p>Today, Vidya represents more than a counselling centre.</p><p>It represents Trupti&#x27;s journey—from working closely with vulnerable communities, to recognising the quieter and less visible mental health struggles within society, and finally creating a space where people from all backgrounds can seek understanding and support.</p><p>What began with a sense of restlessness became a purpose.</p><p>And that purpose continues to guide Trupti&#x27;s work:</p><p>to create a space where people feel heard, understood and accepted—and where seeking help is seen not as a weakness, but as a step towards understanding oneself and living a healthier, more fulfilling life.</p></div></dialog>
<dialog id="privacy"><button class="close" aria-label="Close privacy information">Close ×</button><h2>Privacy information</h2><p>This page does not use analytics, advertising trackers, cookies or browser storage. Information you enter in the enquiry form is used only to prepare a WhatsApp message in your browser.</p><p>When you continue to WhatsApp, the entered name and selected preferences are included in a link sent to WhatsApp. WhatsApp’s own privacy practices apply. The centre receives your message when you send it.</p><p>Please do not include medical records, therapy histories or other sensitive information in an initial message. You may contact the centre directly to ask about how enquiry and session information is handled, retained or deleted, and about confidentiality and its limits.</p><p>Links to maps and social platforms open third-party services with their own privacy practices. Your hosting provider may keep standard access logs.</p></dialog>
<dialog id="terms"><button class="close" aria-label="Close website information">Close ×</button><h2>Website information</h2><p>This website introduces Vidya Counselling Centre and its counselling services. Its content is general information, not an individual assessment, diagnosis or treatment recommendation.</p><p>An enquiry is a request only. Fees, availability, session duration, suitability and appointment confirmation must be agreed directly with the centre. Counselling outcomes vary; no particular result is guaranteed.</p><p>For questions about a service or the information on this website, contact the centre using the details provided.</p></dialog>
